Role write scopes for FILE TOOLS, enforced by tools/agents/guard-write.mjs (PreToolUse hook on Write/Edit/NotebookEdit/MultiEdit). Paths are relative to the guarded repository or one of its worktrees; 'deny' wins over 'allow'; deny patterns match case-insensitively; '.git' segments are never writable. Each reviewer may write only its own record files and its own evidence directory, so concurrently running reviewers cannot alter each other's records or evidence (F-DG0-144). Outside the guarded repository and its worktrees only the run's own private temporary directory (MTH_RUN_TMP) is scratch; the shared /tmp and the home directory never are (D-024, D-028). Shell (Bash) writes are confined separately by the OS sandbox generated by tools/agents/agent_settings.py (D-025). Changing this file is a gate-rule change: it is part of every stage candidate's review scope and implementers cannot edit it.
